{
  "_comment": "MiniMax-H3 FLF on a QUANTISED checkpoint. A byte-for-byte twin of `minimax_h3_flf.json` except for the model loader: `UnetLoaderGGUF` (city96/ComfyUI-GGUF) instead of `UNETLoader`, and no `weight_dtype` \u2014 the GGUF loader does not declare one and sending it fails validation at submit. WHY A SECOND FILE RATHER THAN A FLAG: the stock `UNETLoader` will not even LIST a .gguf, so `resolve()` writing a quantised filename into the safetensors template produces a prompt ComfyUI rejects on an enum \u2014 after the job is claimed. `resolve()` picks the template per mode from model_map, so a GGUF entry names these and nothing else changes. DESKTOP ONLY, deliberately: the studio cloud has no reason to quantise, so these files are not on it. The filenames below are placeholders \u2014 `resolve()` rewrites `unet_name` from the entry's `modes.<mode>.checkpoint` and `clip_name` from its `text_encoders[0]`.",
  "1": {
    "class_type": "UnetLoaderGGUF",
    "inputs": {
      "unet_name": "MiniMax-H3-FL2VA-Q4_K_M.gguf"
    }
  },
  "2": {
    "class_type": "CLIPLoader",
    "inputs": {
      "clip_name": "qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors",
      "type": "minimax",
      "device": "default"
    }
  },
  "3": {
    "class_type": "VAELoader",
    "inputs": {
      "vae_name": "minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors"
    }
  },
  "4": {
    "class_type": "VAELoader",
    "inputs": {
